---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy · Tazk"
  description="How Tazk handles your data: everything stays on your device, no account, and no automatic upload."
>
  <Header lang="en" root="/en/" />
  <main id="main" class="tk-container tk-page tk-prose">
    <h1 class="tk-h2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <time datetime="2026-11">Last updated: November 2026</time>

    <p>
      Tazk is built so your data stays on your device. This page explains what
      is stored, what is not, and when the app touches the network.
    </p>

    <h2>What is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Tasks, habits, subtasks, focus session history, XP, and badges live in a
      local database on your device. There is no account, and there is no copy
      on our servers.
    </p>

    <h2>Network</h2>
    <p>
      Daily use works without internet. The only outgoing connection is the
      <strong>Check for updates</strong> button in Settings: when you press it,
      the app fetches a single JSON file from this page to compare versions.
      You trigger it, and none of your personal data is sent.
    </p>

    <h2>Permissions it may ask for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Notifications</strong>, for task, habit, and focus reminders you
        schedule yourself.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Home-screen widget</strong>, so you can check items without
        opening the app.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Battery optimization exemption</strong> (optional), when Android
        restricts background apps and the widget stops updating. You may
        decline it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>File picker</strong>, only when you export or import a JSON
        backup.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Location</h2>
    <p>
      The place feature on a task opens Maps through a link. Tazk does not read
      GPS and does not store your location.
    </p>

    <h2>No ads and no analytics</h2>
    <p>
      There are no ads, no trackers, and no third-party analytics inside the
      app.
    </p>

    <h2>Backup and restore</h2>
    <p>
      You can export all data to a JSON file at any time and import it back on
      another device. That file belongs entirely to you.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer lang="en" root="/en/" />
</Base>